{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0374","billNumberShort":"H.B. 374","billNumberLong":"HB0374S02","fileNumber":"2026FL1173","shortTitle":"Speech, Language, and Hearing Occupations Licensing Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"BALLAMG","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Ballard, Melissa G.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"VICKEEJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Vickers, Evan J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies the regulations for hearing professionals.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>allows the division to create temporary working groups when no board is available to assist the division;<hr><ltbullet>allows an audiologist to supervise a hearing instrument specialist intern;<hr><ltbullet>repeals the creation of the Speech-language Pathologist and Audiologist Licensing Board;<hr><ltbullet>repeals the exemption permitting an individual to receive licensure as a speech-language pathologist or an audiologist from the State Board of Education;<hr><ltbullet>creates an alternative path for licensure as an audiologist and as a speech-language pathologist;<hr><ltbullet>aligns the unprofessional conduct standards of a hearing instrument specialist with the unprofessional conduct standards of audiologists; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Tyler Moore","fiscalAnalyst":"Noah Matthew Hansen","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/18/2026","trackingID":"XNCSGCXYIB","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-26 10:22:15.960","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","own